    "field:rack::dsp::Upsampler::kernel": {
      "finding": "P1: none of the cited tests checks Upsampler.kernel. In tests/dsp/in_rack_basic/test_resampling.py:124-134 the reference runner returns only [outs, in_index, in_buffer], unlike the decimator runner (line 120), which includes d.kernel.tolist(). test_decimator_and_upsampler (lines 270-277) never reads u.kernel. The uncited test_decimator_and_upsampler_reset (line 296) only compares one RackPy kernel with another, so a view of the wrong array or the wrong length (native/bindings/dsp/resampler.cpp:254) would still pass. Smallest fix: add u.kernel.tolist() to the upsampler reference result in native/tests/dsp_reference.cpp and in the Python runner, as the decimator does, or at least assert len(u.kernel) == OVERSAMPLE*QUALITY plus a value against Rack.",
      "verdict": "finding"
