    "method:rack::dsp::SampleRateConverter::process(const float *, int, int *, float *, int, int *)": {
      "finding": "P1: the binding refuses in_stride or out_stride below channels, and strides below 1 (native/bindings/dsp/resampler.cpp:179-182; documented at docs/reference/dsp.md:546 and in the manifest note), but nothing justifies this. Rack's process (Rack-SDK include/dsp/resampler.hpp:68-99) passes any stride to speex_resampler_set_input/output_stride, or uses it in the copy loop, without asserting. The binding's own size check (inNeed/outNeed = stride*(frames-1) + channels, resampler.cpp:183-184) already keeps every access inside the buffers for any stride of 0 or more, so smaller strides would not crash or be undefined. They are only unusual: overlapping reads, or channels overwriting each other's output. Smallest fix: drop the stride >= channels check (keep only stride >= 0 and the size check), or record a real justification in the doc and the note.",
      "verdict": "finding"
    },
